---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import StandardLifecycleNotice from "../../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import PageToc from "../../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../../data/standards/hgb/drs11.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  subtitle={metadata.nativeTitle}
  framework="hgb"
  status={metadata.status}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "A genuine gap worth naming rather than papering over" },
        { id: "s2", label: "What would resolve this" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Status summary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <StandardLifecycleNotice
    type="draft"
    title="Status Uncertain"
    explanation="Not confirmed — genuinely uncertain"
    link=""
    linkText=""
  />

  <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>A genuine gap worth naming rather than papering over</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card warn">
<div class="ctitle">A genuine gap worth naming rather than papering over</div>
<div class="principle">DRS 11 elaborated related-party disclosure requirements for group accounts, supplementing the general HGB related-party Anhang disclosures. Unlike DRS 7, 8, 9, 10, 12, and 14 — all of which have clearly confirmed, dated successor standards in the DRS 22–27 range — this research did NOT find a clear, confirmed replacement standard specifically for DRS 11's own subject matter. It is possible DRS 11 remains active in some form, was folded into a broader standard without a clean topic-to-topic successor, or was withdrawn without direct replacement (with related-party disclosure left to the general statutory Anhang requirements alone). Rather than assert any of these possibilities with more confidence than the research supports, this entry is presented as a genuine open item.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>What would resolve this</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="cols-1">
    <div class="card info">
<div class="ctitle">What would resolve this</div>
<div class="principle">A direct check of the DRSC's own current standards index (drsc.de/en/pronouncements) would confirm definitively whether DRS 11 remains listed as active, or whether a specific Bundesanzeiger withdrawal notice exists for it — the same verification approach that resolved DRS 6, 7, 9, and others in this series with confidence.</div>
</div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Status summary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="grid col-1">
    <div class="card">
<div class="ctitle">Status summary</div>
<div class="td-table">
<div class="th"><span>Field</span><span>Detail</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Original topic</span><span>Related-party reporting in group accounts</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Current status</span><span>Not confirmed — genuinely uncertain</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Successor</span><span>Not confirmed</span></div>
<div class="tr"><span>Recommended action</span><span>Verify directly against drsc.de before relying on this entry for any specific application</span></div>
</div>
</div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
